designs.correctness:
BY CONSTRUCTION
The attention kernel's math is slidewin_verify_wgmma_kernel<MODE_SPLIT> unchanged:
- S/PV wgmma descriptors, the V^T transpose, Max_offset-8 FP8 P, masks, the partial layout.
- It routes sliding verify B=2..32 on the board (16/16 tests).
- It is self-checked at window 0 on every board import (submission.py:9081-9083: B=1 lens 5000 grid 3; B=2 lens 100/3000 grid 7; B=5 lens 0/7/63/64/4000 kv 0.25 grid 2xSM), at < 2e-2 vs fp32 with e4m3 queries.

Only STG (4 to 5) and IDX_TILES (16 to 8) change, and the ring/meta schedules are written generically in both.

The combine's arithmetic is c320's proven ONEPASS online LSE plus the norm-gate epilogue (routed on full decode_1). Its slot discovery is sw_combine's prefix/owner_of logic (routed). The FP8-P full-layer tail risk (LESSONS 2026-10-25 s3 audit) is covered by Max_offset 8, a coherent-style self-check case and agreement with FA3's output.

CPU EMULATION BEFORE THE BUILD (python, no GPU; the audit reruns it)
(1) Ring/barrier protocol for STG in {4, 5}, IDX_TILES 8 and every per-CTA tile count N = 1..200:
- simulate prologue issues j < STG-1, then the refill at iteration n of nn = n+STG-1, after an EMPTY wait with parity ((n-1)/STG)&1 when n >= 1;
- FULL waits use parity (n/STG)&1;
- assert a stage is refilled only after its previous tile's 256 arrivals;
- assert each wait's parity equals its phase count;
- assert meta block k+1 (issued with tile 8k, landed by the FULL(8k) wait at iteration 8k <= 8(k+1)-(STG-1)) is resident before issue_tile reads it;
- assert block k+2 never overwrites buffer k&1 before tile 8k+7 is issued.
(2) Smem layout for STG 4/5:
- offsets VT 65536/81920 (1024-aligned), BAR 86544/102928 (8-aligned);
- totals 96,096 / 112,496 B;
- 2 x (SMEM_A + 1024) <= 233,472.
(3) Partition against the combine, over random B <= 64, lens (0..8 keys, multiples of 64 +/- 1, 80000, 100000) and grids 1..1024:
- the set of slots the attention kernel writes for request b (bx + cb over CTAs whose range meets b's tiles) equals the combine's {c+b : c in [c_lo, c_hi], vld};
- every slot index < G + B;
- every request has >= 1 slot with finite m (key 0).
(4) The combine's fold in numpy against a direct softmax over synthetic partials: log2 units, the 2^8 offset, -inf slots, 1-slot rows, 264 slots, the same fixed order.

ON THE JUDGE BEFORE ROUTING
- The canary first; each launch announced, then synced and confirmed.
- The 12 B=1 cases per STG: fp32 reference, PDL == plain bitwise, rerun bitwise, error word 0.
- Race agreement vs kernel_fn's FA3 output < 3e-2 (both use e4m3 queries; FA3's own test errors are 0.0795-0.0948 against the 0.15 bound, board records).
- A two-state alternating capture/replay of kernel_fn with refills.

The judge checks every timed call. No test shape enters the route: test 8 (B=1 ctx 1M full verify) is page 64, and the only other full-verify tests have B >= 2.

