spec.correctness:
BY CONSTRUCTION
- The per-tile math is the board's routed sw kernel's: S / PV wgmma, V^T transpose, Max_offset-8 e4m3 P, fp32 online softmax. Only split points and tile alignment change, which only changes fp32 and e4m3-P rounding order.
- The merge is sw_combine_kernel's online LSE in fixed rank order: deterministic and bitwise reproducible, with no atomics.
- PRE=1 reproduces _pre_attention_kernel: scaleless RMS with eps inside the sqrt; interleaved RoPE at positions[t] * inv_freq[i] (fp32 product, as Triton) through rope_sincos (sv1's rows matched Triton's at rel L2 0.00e+00); e4m3 satfinite without 5.473; /k_scale; /v_scale. Only the fp32 summation order differs, so at most 1 code.
- PRE=0 consumes the pre-attention node's own outputs, exactly as today's kernel.
- Key p is in rank 0's new tile for every row, so L > 0.

CPU EMULATOR (numpy, python3 -I; must print PASS per family)
Grid: seq in {0, 1, 7, 8, 16, 63, 64, 65, 1500, 2039, 2040, 2041, 2046, 2047, 2048, 2049, 2055, 2056, 4096, 74000, 80000, 86000, 1048576}; B in {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 16, 32}; C in {4, 8, 16}.
1. Partition: the union over ranks / tiles / masked-valid (token, position), plus the new tile, equals reference.py's window {max(0, p-2047) <= kp <= p} exactly once. Never a page-table read at a position outside [0, seq).
2. Mask predicates equal (1), including the test-gating condition.
3. Full-line and half-line maps write each (row, chunk) of a tile once, to identical SW128 addresses.
4. q words: (g, w, r, tig, word) -> (head, dims) equals the board's qra / qrb addressing. RoPE pair ids per held dim.
5. New-tile bytes (token, head, dim) -> stage-0 address equals what a cp.async of that row would write. Rows 8..63 are zero.
6. Smem offsets, 1024 / 512 alignment, live ranges, the alias (35,840 B in 81,920), total <= 111,712 B.
7. Merge thread -> (row, d0) map at C = 4 / 8 / 16: every output and gate element touched exactly once.
8. Numeric merge: per-rank partials with the 2^8 offset, merged in rank order, match direct softmax to 1e-6 (fp64) and 1e-5 (fp32).
9. FULL / EMPTY arrival counts and parities per phase, for N = 0..9 per CTA, PRE in {0, 1}, including the plain arrivals on FULL[0].
10. IDX entries per CTA <= 512; clamp and zero-fill behaviour.
11. Test-shaped length sets: lognormal mixed B=5 (16..20000), B=3 at about 4000, B=4 at about 6000.
12. rope_sincos vs numpy float64 sin / cos at |a| <= 1.1e5: max abs error <= 2e-7 relative to the range.

PREPARE-TIME GPU CHECKS (before any route)
- attrs: binaryVersion 90, local bytes printed, CTAs/SM 2, clusters per C.
- Named canary: B=2 lens 3 / 2100, C=4, both PRE.
- Matrix, at every candidate (PRE, C) of the band it serves:
  - B=1 lens {0, 7, 1500 at kv 1/64, 2040, 2047, 2048 at kv 0.25, 2056, 80000};
  - B=2 {5, 80000};
  - B=3 {16, 4000, 9000} at kv 1/64 (test 10's shape);
  - B=4 {5800, 6000, 6100, 6200} (test 13);
  - B=5 lognormal mixed {16, 900, 5000, 12000, 20000} (test 3) and {0, 7, 2047, 2048, 60000} at kv 0.25;
  - B=16 _SK_LENS16 with lens16[0..3] = 80000 / 2047 / 2048 / 2055, at kv {1, 0.25, 1/64};
  - B=32 ragged (the _sw_validate set) at kv {1, 0.25, 1/64}.
- Each case must give:
  - rel L2 vs _ps_reference < 2e-2, finite, row-wise worst <= 5x;
  - vs kernel_fn's incumbent output on cloned inputs < 3e-2;
  - PRE=1 new cache rows vs _ps_prepare_q's rows on a cloned cache: e4m3 code gap <= 1, rel L2 < 1e-2;
  - two launches torch.equal;
  - err word 0.
- Two-state replay (_alt_check, gate=_swf_gate, refilled inputs, NaN-poisoned outputs) per routed band.

AUDIT CHECKLIST
- no early return before or between the cluster barriers; every thread reaches every named and cluster barrier;
- generic -> async proxy fence for the thread-written stage 0 (writers fence; consumers fence after the FULL wait);
- ring aliased only after wait_all + wgmma wait + __syncthreads;
- DSMEM reads only between the two cluster barriers;
- satfinite conversions; k_scale and v_scale applied exactly once;
- page indices clamped; position < 0 rows zero-filled;
- no shared-memory write races with the V^T double buffer.

tonight.how:
One check, diag-swf-rungs, on phasec/attn-1028 @ 6851b2d0. A new small load_inline module muse_swf_diag_v1 (sm_90a, -O3 -lineinfo -std=c++20), built inside the first diag function on the import clock. Both kernels use swf's planned dynamic smem (about 111.7 KB) and a cluster cudaLaunchKernelEx.

(a) dg_cmerge<C, MERGE>:
- each CTA loads cache_seqlens[b] cold, then its partial (O [128][64], m, l; some m = -inf) from a torch-made buffer into swf's smem layout (row stride 68);
- MERGE=1 runs the exact swf epilogue: cluster arrive, gate loads, wait, rank-ordered DSMEM reduce-scatter, v_scale / L, scaleless RMSNorm, sigmoid(gate), bf16, second barrier. MERGE=0 finalises its own partial only;
- print MaxActiveClusters and 21-rep cold-L2 medians (null, MERGE=0, MERGE=1); check rel L2 vs a float64 torch rank-order merge < 1e-3.

(b) dg_chain<C, FULLLINE, QPRO> on _ps_synthetic([80000] * B), B = 1 / 16 / 32 at C = 16 / 8 / 4:
- the exact swf prologue: entry loads; seq -> page indices; cp.async of all owned tail-aligned tiles into a 5-stage ring (refill at C=4); wait_all; per-CTA XOR checksum;
- QPRO adds the rope_sincos CS table (copied from d73edd94), the q fragment words (copied out to a debug buffer) and rank 0's new K/V (cache store plus stage-0 rows);
- validate: checksums equal torch's over the same rows; QS bytes within 1 e4m3 code of _ps_prepare_q's q; new rows within 1 code (rel L2 < 1e-2) of the Triton pre-attention's on a cloned cache;
- time null, (half, 0), (full, 0), (full, 1).

Printing: each launch announced and synced; two or three lines, each <= 900 chars, printed after [paths]; start <= 420 s.

Decision rules:
- merge <= 1.2 us at (16,8) and (32,4), and <= 1.0 at (1,16): DSMEM. Above 2.5: the swf-pdl epilogue.
- QPRO delta <= 0.3 us: PRE=1 is expected to lead.
- full/half > 0.97: use the half-line map.
- An occupancy shortfall drops that (B, C).

scores.rationale:
It targets the second-largest headline share (verify 1 sliding, 9.5%) plus the two mid-B sliding verify rows (4.3% + 3.4%). Its mechanism removes measured costs:
- the pre-attention node, 2.8-2.9 us marginal;
- the combine node, 2.7-3.1 us marginal;
- the stream-K prefix machinery.
It keeps the proven tile body. The DSMEM merge form already runs on the board (sliding_cluster_kernel, 9.6 us one-launch decode-1 kernel).

Arithmetic re-derived on the corrected formula:
- design central x1.046 (10.2/14.4/22.4);
- judge central x1.039 (10.8/15.0/23.0): B=1 is pinned to the cluster analog's 10.8 judge net, B=16/32 get a 0.6 us haircut;
- x1.024 even if the fold loses.

Risks:
- it did not know that today's sv1 fold into the B=1 PSEUDO kernel lost (0.934x), so I added a raced PRE=0 arm;
- the sincosf Payne-Hanek local frame would break its 'local 0' milestone, so it uses judge-proven rope_sincos instead.
The big new kernel without a GPU puts P(clean first check, >= 1 band routed) at about 0.55-0.6 with tonight's rungs. EV is about +1.9%.

Rules are safe: no cross-call state, deterministic merge, cluster capture already proven. Size +62 KB on a file with no budget.

spec.summary:
Winner: design 1 (swf), corrected by the judge and then by the red team. Design 2 (fvs) keeps only its zero-new-CUDA rung and a conditional stage 4.

Today's sliding-verify path:
- B=1: 2 graph nodes (pre-attention, then the PSEUDO stream-K kernel with an in-kernel ticket merge).
- B=2..32: 3 nodes (pre-attention, slidewin_verify_wgmma_kernel<SPLIT>, PDL sw_combine_kernel).

swf makes each step ONE cluster launch:
- grid B*C, cluster C = 16 / 8 / 4 by band. These are the only sizes that run in one wave: the judge co-schedules 14 clusters of 16 and about 30 of 8 at this smem. 256 threads (one warpgroup per kv head), 113,888 B smem, 2 CTAs/SM;
- each CTA owns a fixed, tail-aligned slice of the request's 32 old 64-key tiles: 2 / 4 / 8 tiles, which at B=16 / 32 is exactly today's chain of 4 / 8 per CTA. It runs the board's wgmma tile body on them unchanged;
- the 8 new keys are not a ring tile. Rank 0 seeds its online softmax with them in the prologue, while the old tiles are in flight: 2 mma.sync m16n8k32 for S and 8 mma.sync m16n8k16 for PV, about 0.2 us. The board's decode-1 cluster kernel attends its new key the same way, as a separate small mma.sync tile. So no rank's chain exceeds 32/C tiles;
- the C partials merge over DSMEM in fixed rank order with the norm-gate fused. The board's sliding_cluster_kernel already runs this reduce-scatter;
- no workspace, ticket, fence or atomic.

Raced in prepare, per band, against kernel_fn's real (pinned) incumbent:
- PRE=1 folds the pre-attention into the prologue AFTER every gather is issued. PRE=0 keeps today's pre-attention node. PRE=0 is insurance: sv1's fold into the B=1 PSEUDO kernel lost on the judge (16.4 vs 15.3 us, 7284659f) because it sat on the critical path.
- Three launch-time placements: default; the Spread cluster-scheduling policy; and padded smem that forces one CTA per SM where one wave still fits (expected only at B=1). The self-check prints %smid and per-CTA clock64 stamps.

Numbers (corrected formula, board 4e386647 rows):
- central: verify 1 / 16 / 32 sliding 13.90 / 19.51 / 27.10 -> 11.0 / 15.2 / 23.2 us, x1.036;
- best case, everything hidden: 10.8 / 15.0 / 23.0, x1.039;
- low case (the red team's not-hidden case): 12.0 / 17.0 / 25.2, x1.022;
- PRE=0 alone: x1.022;
- from base X's ~1.623 level, the stage-1 check should read about 1.67 (about 1.648 in the low case). Milestones are set at the low case. EV about +1.5%;
- the decode port follows on campaign/eb-trimd, the stripped decode build (the board tree has 1,240 B of room): +0.6-0.9% on decode.

fvs (full verify B=1 on the window kernel at window 0) is built only if its zero-CUDA rung shows that kernel streams 80k keys in <= 14 us. The tile body's ~2 us per tile per SM projects 20-24 us, against FA3's 14.8 us main kernel.

Neither design reaches FA3's full verify at B=16/32 (25.6% of the headline). That needs a faster main loop, which is a separate lever.

spec.angle:
Cut the sliding-verify path's fixed cost at every batch: graph nodes, the pre-attention launch, the separate combine, and the stream-K prefix/ticket machinery. Three constraints come with it:
- no CTA's tile chain grows beyond today's (the new keys ride a register seed on rank 0, not a ring tile);
- where cluster CTAs land is measured and steered;
- the proven tile body is kept, and a no-fold arm insures the fold.
The small-B full-verify work (fvs) is gated on a free diagnostic. FA3's full verify at B=16/32 is out of reach for this tile body.

spec.floor:
TASK.md / reference.speed_of_light_ns, at 4.8 TB/s and 989 TFLOP/s.

verify 1 sliding:
- tokens = 1 x 2048 x 1.0 = 2048;
- bytes = 2048 x 2 x 64 x 2 = 524,288, plus 1 x 8 x 36 x 64 x 2 x 2 = 73,728, total 598,016 B -> 0.125 us;
- FLOPs = 4 x 2048 x 8 x 16 x 64 = 67.1 M -> 0.07 us;
- floor 0.12 us.

verify 16 sliding: tokens = 16 x 2048 x 0.925 = 30,310 -> 7.76 MB, plus 1.18 MB = 8.94 MB -> 1.86 us.

verify 32 sliding: 60,621 tokens -> 17.88 MB -> 3.72 us.

verify 1 full: 80,000 x 256 + 73,728 = 20.55 MB -> 4.28 us.

Practical floor of the one-launch structure with today's tile body:
- one graph node: about 1.0-1.15 us judge;
- the K=8 kernel: 7.6 us import-net. This is three dependent cold round trips (seqlen -> page index -> KV), plus one tile and the store;
- each extra tile on a CTA's chain: about 2.1 us cold. The body is bound per SM;
- chains of 2 / 4 / 8 tiles at C = 16 / 8 / 4. The seed keeps rank 0 at 32/C instead of 32/C + 1;
- merge + norm-gate about 0.5-0.9; fold and seed about 0.4.

So the floor is about 10.5 / 14.8 / 23.2 us import-net with today's body, and swf's centrals (11.0 / 15.2 / 23.2 judge) sit at it. A 3 TB/s-class body would give about 7 / 10 / 13. The leaders' 8-12 us rows at B=16/32 need that faster body, which is the main-loop lever.

spec.mechanism:
MODULE AND LAUNCH
- New load_inline module muse_sliding_verify_fused_v1, sm_90a only: TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=9.0a, -gencode arch=compute_90a,code=sm_90a, -O3 -lineinfo -std=c++20.
- Kernel: swf_kernel<int PRE> (PRE=1 fold, PRE=0 no fold), __launch_bounds__(256, 2), STAGES=5, full-line gather.
- One cudaLaunchKernelEx per step:
  - cudaLaunchAttributeClusterDimension (C,1,1);
  - for placement 1, also cudaLaunchAttributeClusterSchedulingPolicyPreference = cudaClusterSchedulingPolicySpread;
  - dynamicSmemBytes = SMEM_BYTES for placements 0 / 1, or SMEM_PAD = 118,784 B for placement 2 (one CTA per SM; same kernel, no recompile).
- Function attributes, set once per instantiation before any occupancy query:
  - MaxDynamicSharedMemorySize = SMEM_PAD;
  - PreferredSharedMemoryCarveout = 100, as the board's set_attrs does (L5094-5101);
  - NonPortableClusterSizeAllowed = 1 (needed for C=16).
- Indices: b = blockIdx.x / C, rank = blockIdx.x % C. Warpgroup g = kv head; w = warp & 3, r = lane >> 2 (token), tig = lane & 3, hA = 8g + 2w. Row 16w + r is head hA and row 16w + r + 8 is head hA + 1, both token r.

SMEM (base rounded up to 1024)
- RING at 0: 5 stages x 16 KB (K then V, rows of 128 B, SW128: chunk c of row tt at tt*128 + ((c ^ (tt & 7)) << 4)).
- VT at 81,920: [2 heads][2 bufs][4 KB].
- QS at 98,304: u32 [8 words][256 threads], the board's per-thread A-fragment layout.
- CS at 106,496: float2 [8 tokens][32 pairs].
- IDX at 108,544: int32 [8 tiles][64].
- XK at 110,592: [8 keys][144 B]. 128 B are used; the 16-B pad makes the seed's B-fragment loads conflict-free.
- XVT at 111,744: e4m3 [2 heads][64 dims][8 keys].
- FULL[5] and EMPTY[5] at 112,768 (count 256); abort flag at 112,848.
- SMEM_BYTES = 112,864 + 1,024 alignment slack = 113,888, <= 115,712 (2 CTAs/SM; static_assert).
- After the loop, the partials alias the drained ring: O fp32 [128 rows = token*16 + head][stride 68] plus M[128], L[128] = 35,840 B.

DECOMPOSITION (window W=2048, QL=8)
- seq = cache_seqlens[b] - 8. The old keys are [max(0, seq-2047), seq).
- NT = ceil(min(seq, 2047) / 64) old tiles, counted from the end: tile t = positions [seq-64(t+1), seq-64t).
- Rank r owns old tiles [floor(r*NT/C), floor((r+1)*NT/C)): exactly 2 / 4 / 8 at NT=32, C=16/8/4. Rank 0's share is the floor, so rank 0 never has the most tiles.
- Every rank numbers its own tiles v=0..n-1 in the ring, using the board's ring logic with STAGES=5:
  - tiles v=0..4 are in flight before the first wait;
  - at n>=1 the refill nn=n+4 waits EMPTY parity ((n-1)/5)&1;
  - every FULL arrival is a cp.async noinc arrival, on every rank. The protocol is uniform.
- The 8 new keys (positions seq..seq+7) are attended only by rank 0's seed, never by a ring tile.
- Ranks with no tiles skip the loop with m = -inf, l = 0, but still run both cluster barriers.

MASKS
- Old tile t, column ct, token r: valid iff ct >= 64(t+1) - seq AND ct >= 64(t+1) + r - 2047. The test runs only when 64(t+1) > min(seq, 2040).
- New key j: valid for token r iff j <= r.
- Gathers zero-fill rows whose position is < 0 (src-size 0). Page indices are clamped into the cache.

PROLOGUE (the order is the point)
1. Entry:
   - thread 0 inits the mbarriers, then fence.mbarrier_init;
   - all threads issue the independent loads: cache_seqlens[b];
   - PRE=1: own q words (8 x 8 B bf16 from qkv token 8b+r, heads hA and hA+1, dims 32kk + 16jj + 4tig..+3) and positions[8b + (tid>>5)];
   - rank 0, PRE=1: its new k/v pairs (warp = token, lane = RoPE pair: 4 bf16x2) and cache_loc;
   - rank 0, PRE=0: cache_loc[8b+j], then the 8 new K and V cache rows (2 KB, L2-hot: the pre-attention node just wrote them);
   - PRE=0: q8 words (the board's qra/qrb addressing).
2. When seq arrives: plain loads of this CTA's page indices into IDX, then __syncthreads.
3. Issue cp.async for every owned tile that fits the ring (full-line mapping: c = tid & 7, tt = (tid >> 3) + 32j) with noinc arrivals.
4. Only then the fold:
   - PRE=1, CS table: rope_sincos(__fmul_rn((float)positions[8b+j], inv_freq[i])), one entry per thread, then __syncthreads;
   - PRE=1, q: RMS over 64 via quad xor-shuffles (1, 2) (eps inside the sqrt, scaleless), RoPE on the held pairs, e4m3 satfinite without the 5.473 factor, 8 sts32 into QS;
   - PRE=1, rank 0: k = e4m3(RoPE(RMS(k)) / k_scale) and v = e4m3(v / v_scale), both satfinite. Store them to k_cache / v_cache at cache_loc[8b+j]*128 + g*64 + 2l, into XK[j], and into XVT[g][2l, 2l+1][j];
   - PRE=0: sts32 the q8 words. Rank 0 writes XK and XVT from the loaded cache rows.
5. __syncthreads.
6. Rank 0 runs the seed. Other ranks set m = -inf, l = 0, oacc = 0.

THE SEED (rank 0, every warp, before the main loop, while the old tiles are in flight)
- qa from QS, as the loop loads it.
- S: set c[4] = 0. For kk in 0, 1:
  - b0 = lds32(XK + (lane>>2)*144 + g*64 + 32kk + 4tig);
  - b1 = the same address + 16;
  - mma16832(c, qa[kk][0..3], b0, b1). This is the board's e4m3 m16n8k32 helper (_SLIDE_PH_CUDA L4629).
  After both steps, c0, c1 = S[token r, head hA][keys 2tig, 2tig+1], and c2, c3 = the same for head hA+1.
- Softmax:
  - x = c * scale; a key > r gives -inf;
  - row max over the quad (xor 1, 2) = m;
  - P = ex2(x - (m - 8)). This is the tiles' Max_offset-8 scale, so l and O carry the same 2^8;
  - lA = P0 + P1 and lB = P2 + P3 (this lane's columns; the epilogue's quad reduction sums them, as the board does);
  - mA, mB = the two row maxima.
- PV: for nd in 0..7:
  - b0 = cvt.rn.f16x2.e4m3x2 of the 2 bytes XVT[g][8nd + (lane>>2)][2tig, 2tig+1];
  - set d = 0, then mma16816(d, pack_f16x2(P0, P1), pack_f16x2(P2, P3), 0, 0, b0, 0);
  - oacc[4nd + e] = d[e].
- The m16n8k16 accumulator layout equals the wgmma accumulator's per-warp slice: oacc[4nd+e] is row r, dims 8nd+2tig+e, and oacc[4nd+2+e] is row r+8. So the main loop continues the online softmax from this state. The loop's fence_acc + wg_fence before each wgmma order these register writes.
- Cost: 10 mma.sync plus about 30 other instructions per thread, about 0.2 us, under the gather latency (0.8-1.3 us after issue).

MAIN LOOP
The board's per-tile body, copied (base X L8442-8619):
- refill;
- lds32 qa;
- wait FULL, fence.proxy.async;
- 2 S wgmma (desc kst + 64g);
- V^T byte transpose into buffer v&1;
- wg_wait0, EMPTY arrive;
- mask + online softmax with Max_offset 8 in exp2 units;
- pack P to e4m3;
- fence.proxy.async + named_bar(1+g);
- 2 PV wgmma, wg_wait0.
Only the tile -> position map and the mask change. No segment, request, ticket or Q-reload logic.

EPILOGUE
1. cp.async.wait_all, wgmma wait, __syncthreads.
2. Write O, the quad-reduced l and m per row into the ring alias.
3. barrier.cluster.arrive.release; issue gate loads for the rows this rank finalises; barrier.cluster.wait.acquire.
4. Reduce-scatter: rank r finalises rows [r*128/C, (r+1)*128/C), 16 threads per row (one float4 each). Read (m, l, O float4) from ranks 0..C-1 in order (mapa + ld.shared::cluster). Keep a running max M and rescale by ex2(M_old - M_new); m = -inf weighs 0. This is sw_combine_kernel's arithmetic.
5. o * v_scale / L. L > 0 because every row sees key 0 in rank 0's seed. Then scaleless RMSNorm over 64 (xor 8, 4, 2, 1), times sigmoid(gate) with expf, and a bf16 store to out[(8b+j)*1024 + h*64 + d].
6. Second cluster barrier: arrive after the last DSMEM read, wait before exit.
There is no early return anywhere. The bounded mbarrier wait sets the abort flag and err bit 2, then falls through to both cluster barriers.

DEBUG STAMPS (prepare-only)
- Kernel argument long long* dbg, nullptr on every timed or captured launch.
- When it is non-null, thread 0 of each CTA writes 10 int64. Uniform branches only, never inside the main loop:
  - %smid, rank and its tile count;
  - clock64 offsets from CTA entry at: IDX ready, gathers issued, fold done, seed done, first FULL wait returned, loop end;
  - the cycles between the cluster-barrier-1 arrive and the wait's return.
- A cluster's CTAs start together, so the offsets compare across ranks.

GATING
- kernel_fn: `if _SWF_ROUTE and _swf_gate(cfg): return _swf_forward(data)`, right after the sliding-decode block.
- _swf_gate requires: window 2048, q_len 8, page 1, 16/2 heads, d 64, RoPE on, 1 <= B <= 32, and the band in _SWF_ROUTE. _SWF_ROUTE is a MappingProxyType frozen at import: band -> (PRE, C, place).
- Candidates, feasible one-wave cluster sizes only:
  - B=1: PRE {1,0} x C {16,8} x place {0,1,2};
  - B=2..16: PRE {1,0} x C 8 x place {0,1};
  - B=17..32: PRE {1,0} x C 4 x place {0,1};
  - a (C, place) whose MaxActiveClusters at that placement's smem is below the band's largest B is dropped.
- _swf_forward: PRE=0 first calls _sw_prepare_q(data), exactly kernel_fn's pre-attention (SV32 tiled at B=17..32). Then out = torch.empty((B, 8, 1024), bf16) and one swf_attn call.
- _swf_setup runs after _op_setup and before the [paths] re-print:
  1. build;
  2. attrs;
  3. canary;
  4. self-check matrix;
  5. dbg readout (print-only);
  6. per-band gate against kernel_fn with the swf route off. A quick 7-rep pass over the candidates, plus the lens-0 fixed term and a null node, then two interleaved 31-rep cold-L2 rounds for the best two. Route iff both rounds are >= 1.05x (1.03x at B=17..32), the IQR is <= 1.5x the incumbent's, rel L2 vs the incumbent < 3e-2, and the err word is 0;
  7. _alt_check two-state replay with gate=_swf_gate (under _SAY_MUTE);
  8. freeze _SWF_ROUTE.
- Deadlines on the import clock: build start <= 380 s, checks <= 420, final rounds <= 455, replay <= 475.

PDL
None in attention: PRE=1 is one node, and PRE=0 is a plain second node after the pre-attention. Decode (stage 3) PDL-launches the same source after the qkv GEMM, with griddepcontrol.wait after prologue step 3 and launch_dependents after the main loop.

WHY THIS IS NOT tk
- The partials never leave smem: no global write, fence, atomic, counter or reset.
- All C ranks merge, after one hardware cluster barrier.
- C <= 16 and is fixed, independent of the grid.
- tk's merge_head cost +15.8 to +44 us because one 128-thread warpgroup re-read up to 17-264 global slots after an atomic election.

