spec.correctness:
BY CONSTRUCTION
- The per-tile math is the board's routed sw kernel's: S / PV wgmma, V^T transpose, Max_offset-8 e4m3 P, fp32 online softmax. Only split points and tile alignment change, which only changes fp32 and e4m3-P rounding order.
- The seed computes the 8 new keys with the board's decode-1 pattern:
  - e4m3 QK on m16n8k32, over the same e4m3 q and k bytes;
  - fp32 softmax with the tiles' Max_offset-8 scale;
  - f16 P on m16n8k16, with V widened from e4m3;
  - fp32 accumulation.
  Its P is finer than the tiles' e4m3 P.
- The merge is sw_combine_kernel's online LSE in fixed rank order: deterministic and bitwise reproducible, with no atomics.
- PRE=1 reproduces _pre_attention_kernel:
  - scaleless RMS with eps inside the sqrt;
  - interleaved RoPE at positions[t] * inv_freq[i] (fp32 product, as Triton) through rope_sincos (sv1's rows matched Triton's at rel L2 0.00e+00);
  - e4m3 satfinite without 5.473; /k_scale; /v_scale.
  Only the fp32 summation order differs, so at most 1 code.
- PRE=0 consumes the pre-attention node's own outputs.
- Every row has key 0 in rank 0's seed, so L > 0.

CPU EMULATOR (numpy, python3 -I; PASS / FAIL per family; nonzero exit on any FAIL)
Grid: seq in {0, 1, 7, 8, 16, 63, 64, 65, 1500, 2039, 2040, 2041, 2046, 2047, 2048, 2049, 2055, 2056, 4096, 74000, 80000, 86000, 1048576}; B in {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 16, 32}; C in {4, 8, 16}.
1. Partition: the union over ranks / tiles / masked-valid (token, position), plus the seed's (token r, key j <= r), equals reference.py's window {max(0, p-2047) <= kp <= p} exactly once. No page-table read at a position outside [0, seq).
2. Mask predicates equal (1), including the test-gating condition.
3. Full-line and half-line maps write each (row, chunk) of a tile once, to identical SW128 addresses.
4. q words: (g, w, r, tig, word) -> (head, dims) equals the board's qra / qrb addressing. RoPE pair ids per held dim.
5. Seed fragments, modelled from the PTX tables (m16n8k32 e4m3 A / B / C; m16n8k16 f16 A / B / C), on random e4m3 data:
   - S from (qa, XK) equals q . k for (token r, heads hA / hA+1) x 8 keys;
   - PV from (this lane's P, XVT) equals P . V;
   - d[e] lands at the wgmma accumulator's oacc index.
6. XK / XVT bytes per (token, head, dim): the PRE=1 fold and the PRE=0 cache-row loads produce identical bytes. The 144-B XK stride is bank-conflict-free for the seed's loads.
7. Smem offsets, 1024 / 512 / 16 / 8 alignment, live ranges, the alias (35,840 B in 81,920), SMEM_BYTES <= 115,712; SMEM_PAD gives 1 CTA/SM.
8. Merge thread -> (row, d0) map at C = 4 / 8 / 16: every output and gate element touched exactly once.
9. Numeric merge: rank partials (2^8 offset, -inf ranks, rank 0 seeded with f16 P) merged in rank order match a direct softmax with the same roundings to 1e-6 (fp64) and 1e-5 (fp32).
10. FULL / EMPTY arrival counts and parities for N = 0..9 tiles per CTA (noinc arrivals only).
11. IDX entries per CTA <= 512; clamp and zero-fill behaviour.
12. Test-shaped length sets: lognormal mixed B=5 (16..20000), B=3 at about 4000, B=4 at about 6000.
13. rope_sincos vs numpy float64 sin / cos for |a| < 105,615.

PREPARE-TIME GPU CHECKS (before any route)
- attrs: binaryVersion 90, local bytes printed, carveout 100, CTAs/SM 2 at SMEM_BYTES and 1 at SMEM_PAD, MaxActiveClusters per C at both.
- Named canary: B=2 lens 3 / 2100, C=4, both PRE.
- Matrix, at every candidate (PRE, C) of the band it serves (placement never changes results):
  - B=1 lens {0, 7, 1500 at kv 1/64, 2040, 2047, 2048 at kv 0.25, 2056, 80000};
  - B=2 {5, 80000};
  - B=3 {16, 4000, 9000} at kv 1/64 (test 10's shape);
  - B=4 {5800, 6000, 6100, 6200} (test 13);
  - B=5 lognormal mixed {16, 900, 5000, 12000, 20000} (test 3) and {0, 7, 2047, 2048, 60000} at kv 0.25;
  - B=16 _SK_LENS16 with lens16[0..3] = 80000 / 2047 / 2048 / 2055, at kv {1, 0.25, 1/64};
  - B=32 ragged (the _sw_validate set) at kv {1, 0.25, 1/64}.
- Each case must give:
  - rel L2 vs _ps_reference < 2e-2, finite, row-wise worst <= 5x;
  - vs kernel_fn's incumbent output on cloned inputs < 3e-2;
  - PRE=1 new cache rows vs _ps_prepare_q's rows on a cloned cache: e4m3 code gap <= 1, rel L2 < 1e-2;
  - two launches torch.equal;
  - err word 0.
- dbg readout per candidate (PRE, C, place) at the band's gate shape: print-only.
- Two-state replay (_alt_check, gate=_swf_gate, refilled inputs, NaN-poisoned outputs) per routed band.

AUDIT CHECKLIST
- no early return before or between the cluster barriers; every thread reaches every named and cluster barrier;
- the ring is aliased only after wait_all + wgmma wait + __syncthreads;
- DSMEM reads only between the two cluster barriers;
- the seed's fragment maps match emulator family 5; fence_acc + wg_fence before the first wgmma after the seed;
- satfinite conversions; k_scale and v_scale applied exactly once;
- page indices clamped; position < 0 rows zero-filled;
- no shared-memory write races with the V^T double buffer or XK / XVT;
- dbg branches uniform and outside the main loop;
- registers <= 128; prologue / seed / merge state does not overlap sacc.

