  - B=2: {5, 80000};
  - B=3: {16, 4000, 9000} at kv 1/64 (test 10);
  - B=4: {5800, 6000, 6100, 6200} (test 13);
  - B=5: {16, 900, 5000, 12000, 20000} (test 3) and {0, 7, 2047, 2048, 60000} at kv 0.25;
  - B=16: _SK_LENS16 with [0..3] = 80000, 2047, 2048, 2055, at kv {1, 0.25, 1/64};
  - B=32: _sw_validate's lens32 at kv {1, 0.25, 1/64}.
- Pass rule per case:
  - rel L2 vs _ps_reference < 2e-2, finite, worst row <= 5x the mean;
  - vs kernel_fn's incumbent output on CLONED inputs < 3e-2;
  - PRE=1 new cache rows vs _ps_prepare_q's rows on a cloned cache: e4m3 code gap <= 1 and rel L2 < 1e-2 (never bytewise; see LESSONS);
  - a second launch torch.equal;
  - err word 0.
  A failing (PRE, C) is dropped with a printed reason.
- dbg readout (print-only): for every candidate (PRE, C, place) of section 6, at the band's gate shape (B = 1 / 16 / 32, lens 80000), run one eager launch after a 256 MB flush with a dbg buffer. Print one '[swf-lag]' line per band. Per candidate it gives:
  - the distinct SMs / CTAs and the max CTAs per SM;
  - lag0 = the median over clusters of (rank 0's first-FULL-return minus the median of the other ranks'), in us at the device clock;
  - wait1 = the median barrier-1 wait of ranks != 0.

